<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42425" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sălūtĭger</span></b> ,
			gĕra, gĕrum, adj.
		salusgero (post-class.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Health-bringing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Juppiter,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 8, 26</span></i>
			 (cf. salutaris, II. <i>fin.</i>): ortus, Prud.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ.</span> 11,
			235.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>That brings a greeting</i>, <i>salutatory</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">libelli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 25, 4</span></i>
			.—Hence, <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sălūtĭger</span></b> ,
				gĕri, m., <i>one who delivers a greeting; a messenger</i>, <i>servant</i>, <i><span class="en">App. de Deo Socr. p. 45,
				24</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
